Vries</surname> <given-names>P</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Livermore</surname> <given-names>MTJ</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Bradley</surname> <given-names>DJ</given-names></string-name>, <etal/> Climate change and future populations at risk of malaria. Global Environmental Change. <year>1999</year>;9:S89&#x02013;1S107.</citation></ref><ref id="R12"><label>12. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Zhou</surname> <given-names>G</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Minakawa</surname> <given-names>N</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Githeko</surname> <given-names>AK</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Yan</surname> <given-names>G</given-names></string-name> <article-title>Association between climate variability and malaria epidemics in the East African highlands.</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A</source> <year>2004</year>;<volume>101</volume>:<fpage>2375</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>80</lpage> <pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1073/pnas.0308714100</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14983017</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R13"><label>13. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Shanks</surname> <given-names>GD</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Biomndo</surname> <given-names>K</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Maguire</surname> <given-names>J</given-names></string-name> <article-title>Travel as a risk factor for malaria requiring hospitalization on a highland tea plantation in western Kenya.</article-title><source>J Travel Med</source> <year>2004</year>;<volume>11</volume>:<fpage>354</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15569571</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R14"><label>14. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Vittor</surname> <given-names>AY</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Gilman</surname> <given-names>RH</given-names></s